cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "transport-bus-cli: the command line as a transport layer"
abstract: >
  A transport layer whose wire is a terminal. It sends one command over the
  harness command bus and prints the interactor's CBOR reply, so the interactors
  can be driven with no container, no registry and no cold start -- everything
  below the input is what a RunPod worker does.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/transport-bus-cli"
keywords:
  - cli
  - transport
  - iceoryx2
  - shared-memory

references:
  - type: software
    title: "contract-bus: the weft plane harness"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/contract-bus"
    notes: >
      Vendored as third_party/harness by git subtree. Its Python bus module is
      the client half this uses, and belongs upstream in that repository.

  - type: software
    title: "transport-runpod: the RunPod Serverless transport layer"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/transport-runpod"
    notes: >
      The same bus client, in front of a queue instead of a terminal. A command
      that works here works there, which is what makes this worth having.

  - type: software
    title: "iceoryx2: lock-free zero-copy inter-process communication"
    authors:
      - name: "Contributors to the Eclipse Foundation"
    year: 2026
    version: "0.9.3"
    license: Apache-2.0
    url: "https://github.com/eclipse-iceoryx/iceoryx2"
    notes: >
      The bus, through its PyPI binding, pinned to the version contract-bus
      transcribed its C ABI from.
